\documentclass{article}
\title{Rough Volatility Models for Option Pricing}
\author{Alex Wang}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Option pricing models has evolved rapidly in the last decade. The rough volatility model capture the scaling behavior of real markets. In the past, classical models fails to reproduce the volatility smile. Our method do not require a large dataset for calibration. These result shows that the implied volatility surface can be fitted with few parameters.
\section{Model}
We model the volatility process with a fractional Brownian motion.
\end{document}
